{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed","id":624930,"title":"Silver Fangs and minimum Pure Breed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-12T19:15:55-07:00","id":624930,"title":"Silver Fangs and minimum Pure Breed","content":"I've been thinking about Silver Fangs and the minimum Pure Breed to be one. Is PB 3 the minimum because that is currently the minimum the existing Silver Fangs line are? If so, then we have a situation where theoretically in the future Silver Fang Pure Breed could fall down to 2 or even 1, or perhaps even zero by the end times. In other words, the limit reflects the current &quot;genetic&quot; drift of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Or is it that Falcon simply won't accept anyone with Pure Breed lower than 3? In other words, it is a requirement of the Totem.<br /> <br /> Or that it is a choice by the existing Silver Fang lines that anyone with less than PB 3 won't be allowed to participate in the tribal Rite of Passage. In other words, it's a function of Silver Fang society.<br /> <br /> I ask because I am working on some Silver Fang kinfolk plot, and I began wondering how the tribe would react to a particular kinfolk family whose Pure Breed maybe declining under 3, or perhaps already has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T19:28:09-07:00","id":624972,"title":"","content":"I remember reading somewhere that the tribe rejects cubs with a Pure Breed of less than 3. Both of the Dark Ages lines used a 3 so I doubt genetic drift is responsible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T21:04:18-07:00","id":625056,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed is as much spiritual/mystical as it is physical (as it is with all things in terms of the Garou), so it's less to do with &quot;genetic drift&quot;, alone, as it is the balance of circumstances: how often are the homid and lupus sides &quot;balanced&quot; along a given werewolf's lineage? -- how much time has the breeding family spent in the Umbra/in the physical world (as an ongoing average, not necessarily month-to-month or even year-to-year)? -- how good a terms are they on with Falcon, as well as spirits in general? -- does the garou's lineage include a number of &quot;heroic&quot;/well-Renowned forefathers, as well as many kinfolk who themselves have interbred for generations on end? All of those things are factors. Genetics are important, but they are quite literally only half (and sometimes a little less than that) of the equation when determining the Pure Breed of a particular Garou. That's why, even though they have many in-bred defects, the Silver Fangs maintain such a Pure Breed standing, despite &quot;genetics&quot; indicating that they &quot;shouldn't&quot;. That's why even Metis -- particularly in the Dark Ages and earlier, assuming they survived the pack/tribe -- can have Pure Breed -- they still may possess spiritual/mystical factors that play above the &quot;faulty&quot; genetics that they have... though, of course, the reverse can be true, and a weakening spiritual lineage can require mundane genetics to &quot;pick up the slack&quot;... which, for many outside the Silver Fangs -- particularly the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers and Red Talons -- is a bad sign as the human/lupus blood ratio is very dangerously thin for those groups, particularly the GW (who lack lupus) and the RT (some of whom are so removed from humans that their Homid form more closely resembles their Neanderthal heritage than Homo Sapiens... talk about thin/removed blood! -- they'd make a 15th generation vampire look good...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T07:29:09-07:00","id":625477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=624972#post624972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere that the tribe rejects cubs with a Pure Breed of less than 3. Both of the Dark Ages lines used a 3 so I doubt genetic drift is responsible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my take on it as well. Of course a Silver Fang can screw some human and produce a bastard, but neither the tribe nor Falcon will accept them as one of their own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:32:22-07:00","id":625807,"title":"","content":"The point is, that in-character the garou don't know that Pure Breed is a trait that has a value of 0 to 5. So, Pure Breed, as in being exemplary of your tribe, is a self fulfilling-prophecy.<br /> <br /> That said, for all the stuff I liked about Black Fury revised, I hated that it stated that their are black furred Silver Fangs out there, for such a creature would not be exemplary of the tribe of Falcon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T14:33:30-07:00","id":625937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=625807#post625807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, that in-character the garou don't know that Pure Breed is a trait that has a value of 0 to 5. So, Pure Breed, as in being exemplary of your tribe, is a self fulfilling-prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't know it as a scaled value of &quot;0-5&quot;, as such, but in-narrative they *do* intuitively sense/know when a werewolf is pure-bred or not (this is referenced in a number of books), and the Silver Fangs (of *all garou*) certainly know when one is &quot;up to snuff&quot;, breed-wise, even if they don't conceptualize it as &quot;oh, he's only a 2 -- <i>sooo close</i>, but not *quite* good enough...&quot; -- they'd only sense/pick up on the latter part of that statement, vs. the numeric aspect. The trait is metaphysical as much as it is genetic, which is why even the BSDs respond to it when they encounter a pure-bred garou (it may not stop them from trying to kill/corrupt him, of course, but they do show an appropriate level of subtle deference/respect to the pure-bred wolf...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:04:22-07:00","id":626022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=625807#post625807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, that in-character the garou don't know that Pure Breed is a trait that has a value of 0 to 5. So, Pure Breed, as in being exemplary of your tribe, is a self fulfilling-prophecy.<br /> <br /> That said, for all the stuff I liked about Black Fury revised, I hated that it stated that their are black furred Silver Fangs out there, for such a creature would not be exemplary of the tribe of Falcon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fosterage is notunheard of in noble families, I don't feel so unlikely that a male cub refused by virtue of his gender coudl be deemed worthy by Falcon, if pure-bred enough<br /> That said, TB: Black Furies was Revised, and W20 clearly specifies that Pure Breed is also a result of the cub's ancestors pledging fealty to the same tribe for generations. I think it also mentions somewhere that if a cub chooses a tribe they were not born into, or if a Garou undergoes the Rite of Renunciation, then any PB from the &quot;parent&quot; tribe is forfeit; so that line in TB:BF is really out of date. Make of that what you will, I think it's an unnecessary revision...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T21:36:28-07:00","id":626297,"title":"","content":"Thanks for everyone's answer. There seems to be strong consensus it is a function of Silver Fang culture. Once the First Change happens, they can sense the new cub is under their minimum standard, and therefore pawn it off on some other tribe.<br /> <br /> However, it has an interesting implication. What if there is a &quot;rogue&quot; Silver Fang who knows the Rite of Passage and performs the rite for a PB 2 (or even lower) Garou of Silver Fang descent who has achieved his quest. There is nothing that prevents that except custom and tradition. Other Silver Fangs could punish the rogue ritemaster and inferior Silver Fang cliath, but there is nothing that could undo the Rite. The PB2 Garou would still be a child of Falcon with access to all the tribal Gifts. Would the tribe turn the Garou into a Ronin? That's the only thing I could see the tribe doing to prevent this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T01:31:26-07:00","id":626427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=626297#post626297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, it has an interesting implication. What if there is a &quot;rogue&quot; Silver Fang who knows the Rite of Passage and performs the rite for a PB 2 (or even lower) Garou of Silver Fang descent who has achieved his quest. There is nothing that prevents that except custom and tradition. Other Silver Fangs could punish the rogue ritemaster and inferior Silver Fang cliath, but there is nothing that could undo the Rite. The PB2 Garou would still be a child of Falcon with access to all the tribal Gifts. Would the tribe turn the Garou into a Ronin? That's the only thing I could see the tribe doing to prevent this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be a member of a Tribe, the tribal Totem has to accept them. I don't believe Falcon would accept the cub in this case, and so I don't actually see this situation happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:16:42-07:00","id":626495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=626427#post626427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be a member of a Tribe, the tribal Totem has to accept them. I don't believe Falcon would accept the cub in this case, and so I don't actually see this situation happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The spiritual half is just as important as the physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:40:56-07:00","id":627163,"title":"","content":"So you two disagree with the others that it is case where it is the tribe members that reject the cubs. Instead, it is the Tribal Totem.<br /> <br /> The question is why does a spirit care about Pure Breed?<br /> <br /> If Pure Breed is generated as a result of your heroic ancestors, then the first Garou had no Pure Breed. Why did Falcon accept those first Garou? If you believe all of the first Garou had Pure Breed 5, then how could this degenerate over time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T19:01:50-07:00","id":627172,"title":"","content":"I very much think it's the Totem. Albrecht was rejected by his tribe, but remained a Silver Fang. Falcon didn't disown him.<br /> <br /> Not all spirits care about Pure Breed, but some certainly do. It is a (semi-)mystical trait. Some spirits value it. Some don't care. Falcon certainly cares.<br /> <br /> And just because the first Garou were Pure Breed 5 wouldn't have anything to do with whether or not they can lose it over time. It more than likely remained high for a good long while (centuries? millennia?). Eventually, breeding with humans (for both Garou and Kin), not living up to your ancestors deeds, and/or switches tribes will all take it's toll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:11:46-07:00","id":627612,"title":"","content":"Before the tribes formed the Garou functioned as a single tribe, once they began to split and formed tribes certain factors began to come into play: Black Furies, no males-Totem ban. Red Talons, no homids- Totem ban. Silver Fangs Pure Breed 3 minimum for Falcon to accept same sort of deal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:27:08-07:00","id":627918,"title":"","content":"Some are spiritual, some are social. Griffin will <i>not</i> accept a Homid into his ranks. Period. Even if some wacky Red Talon tried to bring a Homid into the tribe, all that would likely happen is a dead homid cub and a severely punished Red Talon. On the other hand, Wendigo doesn't seem to really give a good goddamn so long as you're ferocious and willing to respect animistic peoples, but the Wendigo tribe are very caught up in homid lineage; So while hte totem might very well see a Zulu warrior dude as being a cool guy, the wendigo elders simply wouldn't offer him a Rite of Passage.<br /> <br /> The Pure Breed thing for Fangs is spiritual. As noted, Garou don't know Pure Breed follows a scale of 0 - 5 (or higher, with some totems... go figure) and so even the Fangs themselves couldn't really make that call. But Falcon can. and an insufficiently well-bred Garou can get rejected out of hand. <i>Interestingly</i>, it is the tribal totem that decides whether breeding &quot;works&quot; or not... meaning that it is actually possible for the Revised Fury book example to work - a Male Fury from a sufficiently heroic bloodline MIGHT actually be able to &quot;get the nod&quot; from Falcon, if he sought to join.. .but in <i>that</i> case he'd have to convince the tribe to even give him the opportunity...it's happened in the past (you don't get 16 sub-tribes through hte power of incest, after all) so it's possible it could happen again. Too bad all the other Garou are insufficiently heroic, and the oens with such strong blooddlines are under enormous pressure to &quot;keep it local&quot; themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:24:57-07:00","id":628032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=625937#post625937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wouldn't know it as a scaled value of &quot;0-5&quot;, as such, but in-narrative they *do* intuitively sense/know when a werewolf is pure-bred or not (this is referenced in a number of books), and the Silver Fangs (of *all garou*) certainly know when one is &quot;up to snuff&quot;, breed-wise, even if they don't conceptualize it as &quot;oh, he's only a 2 -- <i>sooo close</i>, but not *quite* good enough...&quot; -- they'd only sense/pick up on the latter part of that statement, vs. the numeric aspect. The trait is metaphysical as much as it is genetic, which is why even the BSDs respond to it when they encounter a pure-bred garou (it may not stop them from trying to kill/corrupt him, of course, but they do show an appropriate level of subtle deference/respect to the pure-bred wolf...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is more likely the later statement, but I think it is neither.<br /> Pure Breed is sublime in nature, and it can't be sensed by itself. It being sensed only manifests in social circumstances, where the pure bred person has an edge over those of lesser breeding and equal social abilities and attributes.<br /> Meaning, if you had two garou and a number of neutral garou guinea-pigs and you would have the two garou try to incite the neutral guinea-pig-garou it might come to pass that both have the same dice pool and score the same amount of successes to do the inciting. Just because one has more Attribute/Ability to compensate for the Pure Breed bonus dice. In the end, it is the question, can the guinea-pig-garou tell whether a success is from a Pure Breed die or a Charisma die. I think, they can not. I think both successes feel to them equally.<br /> <br /> So, what I'm saying, is that I believe that while In-Game there are no Silver Fangs with Pure Breed below 3 and while I believe that is because of the Silver Fang society discarding those who are not suitable, I still believe that the garou can't distinguish the Pure Breed rating from the attributes the character in question has.<br /> The rating limit is solely enforced by the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=626022#post626022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fosterage is notunheard of in noble families, I don't feel so unlikely that a male cub refused by virtue of his gender coudl be deemed worthy by Falcon, if pure-bred enough</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, that I read ahead and you already mentioned some parts of the stuff I was gona writing.<br /> But, there is another thing. Pure Breed means you are a paragon on your respective tribe. The higher the Pure Breed the more you should stick to the archetypes of the tribe and the more you share the obvious characteristics of the tribe, including the physical ones.<br /> Black Fur and Snow-white Fur (which has mystical significance for the tribe) are not even close, they are actually quite opposed to each other. While a Pure Breed 0 character with characteristics of another tribe works in pretty much every tribe, it does not work with the Silver Fangs for they have no garou who are &quot;low on the characteristics of the tribe&quot;. They only have Pure Breed 3+ members. Members that don't share the characteristics of the tribe therefore can't be members of the Silver Fang tribe.<br /> <br /> That's what I meant (amongst other things) when calling Pure Breed a self-fulfilling prophecy. The Pure Breed makes you share the characteristics of the Silver Fangs, which make you a Silver Fang, which grants you Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=626022#post626022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, TB: Black Furies was Revised, and W20 clearly specifies that Pure Breed is also a result of the cub's ancestors pledging fealty to the same tribe for generations. I think it also mentions somewhere that if a cub chooses a tribe they were not born into, or if a Garou undergoes the Rite of Renunciation, then any PB from the &quot;parent&quot; tribe is forfeit; so that line in TB:BF is really out of date. Make of that what you will, I think it's an unnecessary revision...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was already the case in revised and in 2nd Editon, the most prominent case the Black Spiral Dancers and their hard Pure Breed limit of 5 or nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=627163#post627163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you two disagree with the others that it is case where it is the tribe members that reject the cubs. Instead, it is the Tribal Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They both do. Society wouldn't let a person with not enough pure breed apply for the tribe and even if one did due to unforeseen circumstances Falcon would not accept the applicant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=627163#post627163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is why does a spirit care about Pure Breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, he has strict idea of how his tribe has to be. And every member has to be more than 100% in line with this idea. Every person that is, has this &quot;being an exemplar specimen of the tribes ideals&quot; status if form of a rule mechanics trait - that is Pure Breed. If you don't have that trait, you don't have the mindset, virtue, soul, body and general ability to be a Silver Fang proper, ergo Falcon doesn't let you join.<br /> <br /> That said, most tribes have certain qualities they want from their members. These are tested in either the Rite of Passage or the Rite of Adoption, <b>and before.</b> For only those who have undergone some tutoring are allowed to start the Rites in question. And it would be an unhonourable and careless act to not be thorough in evaluation an applicant before such a Rite and let the Totem decide. The Totem is your GOD, and if you can't find the qualities needed in the tribe in other, maybe you shouldn't be in the tribe either.<br /> <br /> And that said, I believe, a renegade Silver Fang could not simply enact the rite and make an applicant with too little Pure Breed a Silver Fang. The Rite requires in my opinion some kind of community to work. It is not specified in W20 with the Rites or Rites of Renown entries, respectively, but it is imo subtext.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=627163#post627163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Pure Breed is generated as a result of your heroic ancestors, then the first Garou had no Pure Breed. Why did Falcon accept those first Garou? If you believe all of the first Garou had Pure Breed 5, then how could this degenerate over time?</div> </div> </div> </div>The statement, that it is granted by the heroic ancestors is simply not true. It is granted by the character creation process and the ST - no one else. It is however said, that if one has pure breed, one has not only the characteristics of the tribe within one's blood, body, soul and mindset, but is most likely from a linage of garou who did so, too.<br /> <br /> That said, the first garou surely were paragon of what it meant to be garou. But they bred with humans and wolfs alike, who were not. Their children either were born with the same physical, mental and spiritual characteristics that are represented in pure breed, or with fewer. Just as today, there are some born, who's pure breed outgrows their parents, or is lower, or is the same. But Pure Breed is a trait of the character who has it, which is almost every time found to be in a linage where it is also present in ancestors, but an individuals score is just a trait for that individual.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:38:34-07:00","id":628044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=627172#post627172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much think it's the Totem. Albrecht was rejected by his tribe, but remained a Silver Fang. Falcon didn't disown him.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be precise (and by that I mean, what I remember from the book I read ages ago): Albrecht was rejected by his Great-Grandfather, who had every one convinced Albrecht was his Grand-Child (for purposes of inheritance). Albrecht was is proud an joy and heir apparent until the day when he appeared to become to much of a threat to his still reigning Great-Grandfather - the King. He was then banished from the sept and protectorate, but not from the tribe. There is no mention that any Rite was enacted to make him loose his tribal membership. There wouldn't have been grounds to enact such a Rite, which would be a Punishment Rite, in the first place - for even Silver Fang don't throw garou out of the tribe, when they present the carcass of a mighty wyrm beast in the throne room, no matter the stench.<br /> Albrecht could have gone to another Silver Fang sept an be their hero, but he chose to hide at the bottom of a bottle instead. That certainly is unbecoming for a Silver Fang and might have cost him additional sympathies with his former sept-mates, but that is another story.<br /> <br /> Actually, I as ST wouldn't allow a Pure Breed 4 garou-PC to act this way for a prolonged time span, since their Pure Breed should make the paragons of their tribe and even with with the Silver Fangs mental issues one should strive to be better sooner, rather than later. But, it makes for a nice drama story, so I can look past that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 08-15-2015, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T21:50:10-07:00","id":628203,"title":"","content":"Albrecht was cast out by the &quot;king&quot; of House Wyrmfoe, no other Silver Fang Sept would take him and in his own mind this means Falcon has rejected him. Also Albrecht had his Pure Breed mystically enhanced by the spirit within the Silver Crown. His banishment was the reason for the duel between himself and Arkady which set up the whole Silver Crown story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T22:54:28-07:00","id":628237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628032#post628032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed is sublime in nature, and it can't be sensed by itself. It being sensed only manifests in social circumstances, where the pure bred person has an edge over those of lesser breeding and equal social abilities and attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628032#post628032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, there is another thing. Pure Breed means you are a paragon on your respective tribe. The higher the Pure Breed the more you should stick to the archetypes of the tribe and the more you share the obvious characteristics of the tribe, including the physical ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these two statements are somewhat contradictory and would be interested in hearing how you reconcile them. I do agree that when it comes to &quot;rolling&quot; your Charisma + Ability + Pure Breed, that the target can't distinguish one from the other, only the effect. However, I think it can be determined by other means than simply the effect of certain social circumstances. In a real sense, Garou inherently know whether another Garou has better PB than himself - I think it is instinctive animal nature that causes a lower PB to naturally defer to a greater one, although the full effects aren't notice until social challenges start being called.<br /> <br /> However, clearly Tribes can make some kind of distinction between the various levels of Pure Breed, even if they don't use the game mechanics determination of ranks 1-5. A big part of the Silver Fangs is that they know Pure Breed is declining and know which specific family lines have more than others. That is why some Silver Fang families practice inbreeding to various degrees, including incest, to keep that level of standard. They may not rank them according to 1-5, but there are characteristics of what a PB5 (for every tribe) should look like in the same way Dog Show judges can evaluate this specific dog is what this kind of dog breed should look like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628032#post628032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the first garou surely were paragon of what it meant to be garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the very first Garou, the first Garou born in the Paleolithic Ice Age who knew nothing about the spirit world and had to earn their hard won knowledge, the ones who figured out the very first ways to make pacts to get Gifts and Rituals, were born with Pure Breed 5, I believe they had zero Pure Breed. I believe what would become Pure Breed was something that was generated as the first generations of Garou produced the heroes of myth and legend - the ones who stole fire from Helios, made the first pacts with Falcon and other spirits, established the first caerns, etc. Their personal characteristics were prized as signs that newborn Garou had that same power and excellence of their forefathers, And this is what helped generate the effects of Pure Breed. I don't think all the first Garou had this. Some ice age Garou were awesome. Some ice age Garou didn't do jack. Eventually, as the best/alphas were distinguished from the worst/omegas family lines over time, then Pure Breed emerged as a real property, supported by spiritual/magical ties. This might have taken centuries or even thousands of years.<br /> <br /> This is how I figure it out anyway. I understand if others choose something else. Most players likely never bother to think about these kind of things because in most games, it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> For me I am thinking about this because I am considering of running a subplot where a particular SF kinfolk family is now at the point that they can only produce Garou who have Pure Breed 2. Therefore, I'm trying to figure out what this means, and how other Garou will react to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T02:23:34-07:00","id":628411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628203#post628203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Albrecht was cast out by the &quot;king&quot; of House Wyrmfoe, no other Silver Fang Sept would take him and in his own mind this means Falcon has rejected him. Also Albrecht had his Pure Breed mystically enhanced by the spirit within the Silver Crown. His banishment was the reason for the duel between himself and Arkady which set up the whole Silver Crown story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The King of one house. Surely other Silver Fangs would realise why such a banishment came to pass, but the other houses would not owe fealty to house Wyrmfoe - and pissing them off might just have been a low price for a formidable fighter of high pure breed...<br /> The reason for the duel was Arkady howling long during the mourning for the King, which was a challenge to Albrecht and his right to succeed the King. Although the whole &quot;heir&quot; thing is kind of questionable when &quot;the leader may be challenged at any time during peace&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628237#post628237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think these two statements are somewhat contradictory and would be interested in hearing how you reconcile them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both statements relate to different aspects of Pure Breed, but aren't exclusive to each other. Also, I wrote &quot;sublime&quot; when wanting to write &quot;subliminal&quot; - not a native speaker, didn't know &quot;sublime&quot; was a word and what it meant.<br /> So, the effect of Pure Breed is subliminal to others. They react to it and can't help to do so (except for some Stargazer Willpower boost gift, iirc). But the very core of subliminal is, that they can't wittingly sense it in most circumstances. Exceptions being possible, especially if the difference between you and the pure bred character is HUGE.<br /> The other statement is what Pure Breed means for the character, who has it. And there Pure Breed is a certain character trait, that has to be represented by role-playing (especially in LARP). It is more than the dots on the sheet. It is a obligation the player has to portrait his character with certain characteristics - for he choose to have these as part of his character. That two can be regarded as subliminal, if you think of Pure Breed as something forced on the normal mindset of the character. But I don't see it that way, I thing it is something that is part of the characters psyche inherently. Just as his Nature, his Auspice (that usually brings some characteristics to the character) and every other part of the PC's characteristics. It is &quot;sharing the tribes physical, social and mental trademarks&quot; with a score, rather than just &quot;belonging to the tribe&quot; contra &quot;not belonging to the tribe&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628237#post628237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree that when it comes to &quot;rolling&quot; your Charisma + Ability + Pure Breed, that the target can't distinguish one from the other, only the effect. However, I think it can be determined by other means than simply the effect of certain social circumstances. In a real sense, Garou inherently know whether another Garou has better PB than himself - I think it is instinctive animal nature that causes a lower PB to naturally defer to a greater one, although the full effects aren't notice until social challenges start being called.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue, that only larger differences in Pure Breed scores can be instinctively sensed. Differences of one (maybe two) might fall under the bus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628237#post628237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, clearly Tribes can make some kind of distinction between the various levels of Pure Breed, even if they don't use the game mechanics determination of ranks 1-5. A big part of the Silver Fangs is that they know Pure Breed is declining and know which specific family lines have more than others. That is why some Silver Fang families practice inbreeding to various degrees, including incest, to keep that level of standard. They may not rank them according to 1-5, but there are characteristics of what a PB5 (for every tribe) should look like in the same way Dog Show judges can evaluate this specific dog is what this kind of dog breed should look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is 0 to 5. But sure, the Silver Fangs, as the humans, do know that certain characteristics may be lost, due to breeding with people who have other characteristics. It didn't need George Mendel and his peas to make that common knowledge - simple observation was enough.<br /> And there could be a long discussion, if the &quot;incest claim&quot; is true or not. Revised Edition granted the Silver Fangs a rite to find the household with the perfect partner. Might still mean, that you could pick wrong (Sorry, horny boy, your perfect mate is not sexually active until you are 25 / Sorry Prince, your perfect mate isn't the lords legitimate daughter, but her bastard cousin who works in the kitchen). And there might be people who simply ignore the Rite, have no Theurge to perform it, marry their kin relatives for political reasons since the Rite does not work on them and so on. So, all the other tribes see the optional tribal weakness flaw quirks (and sometimes Fish-Malk tendencies) and believe the Silver Fangs go mad because of incest. But revised also tells us, that the madness of their prominent members (their leaders) is due to a Curse, not incest (unless you consider the latter to be a Curse, too).<br /> <br /> But you are right, garou could try to evaluate the pure breed of others on physical and mental characteristics and relating them to reference points - like dog show judges. Would be subjective, but possibly relatively accurate, if the garou who does so is experienced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628237#post628237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the very first Garou, the first Garou born in the Paleolithic Ice Age who knew nothing about the spirit world and had to earn their hard won knowledge, the ones who figured out the very first ways to make pacts to get Gifts and Rituals, were born with Pure Breed 5, I believe they had zero Pure Breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> We could at this point start a complete discussion about the Dawn Times, and how the were or not. I'm going to say, that in these times the Gauntlet was possibly not yet in existence and the first garou was like the rest of the world a being of both flesh and spirit. And like a spirit, who has a type and very specific characteristics, the garou had too.<br /> And while &quot;Pure Breed&quot; is tribal specific and there weren't tribes around back then, the garou might have had something different, like &quot;Pure Garouishness&quot; that would turn into &quot;Pure Breed&quot; once specific characteristics (or lack thereof) were established for certain tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=628237#post628237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I believe what would become Pure Breed was something that was generated as the first generations of Garou produced the heroes of myth and legend - the ones who stole fire from Helios, made the first pacts with Falcon and other spirits, established the first caerns, etc. Their personal characteristics were prized as signs that newborn Garou had that same power and excellence of their forefathers, And this is what helped generate the effects of Pure Breed. I don't think all the first Garou had this. Some ice age Garou were awesome. Some ice age Garou didn't do jack. Eventually, as the best/alphas were distinguished from the worst/omegas family lines over time, then Pure Breed emerged as a real property, supported by spiritual/magical ties. This might have taken centuries or even thousands of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T03:19:16-07:00","id":628420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=627163#post627163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you two disagree with the others that it is case where it is the tribe members that reject the cubs. Instead, it is the Tribal Totem.<br /> <br /> The question is why does a spirit care about Pure Breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a spirit is an embodiment of certain concepts. Falcon is basically &quot;the birthright to rule&quot;, whereas Grandfather Thunder is &quot;the fitness to rule&quot;. And each one of these will have certain prerequisites when it comes to proper followers of their tribe,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Pure Breed is generated as a result of your heroic ancestors, then the first Garou had no Pure Breed. Why did Falcon accept those first Garou? If you believe all of the first Garou had Pure Breed 5, then how could this degenerate over time? </div> </div> </div>Take a look at the founding myth of the Silver Fangs: Wolf saved Gaia from the Wyrm and died in the process. When he was revived, his fur had turned silver and Falcon sponsored him. He set the standard that modern Pure Breed is derived from.<br /> (Since almost nothing is known about the creation of the Garou except for their legends of it, I'd consider it rather unproductive to speculate about them in evolutionary terms as primitive near-apes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:17:25-07:00","id":628585,"title":"","content":"The two strongest houses in North America are Wyrmfoe and Unbreakable Hearth the other houses may have representation but the two biggies are Unbreakable Hearth and Wyrmfoe. Wyrmfoe controls the Northeast, the region in question with regards to Albrecht. Arkady's pure breed also played into the duel and made him a viable contender for the throne of House Wyrmfoe despite being from a different House.<br /> <br /> The stories aside, I like to think of the background bans being something that has meaning. Silent Striders the curse of Set, Bans from tribal totems, or a reaction from a social standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T22:56:56-07:00","id":629581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed?p=627172#post627172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much think it's the Totem. Albrecht was rejected by his tribe, but remained a Silver Fang. Falcon didn't disown him.<br /> <br /> Not all spirits care about Pure Breed, but some certainly do. It is a (semi-)mystical trait. Some spirits value it. Some don't care. Falcon certainly cares.<br /> <br /> And just because the first Garou were Pure Breed 5 wouldn't have anything to do with whether or not they can lose it over time. It more than likely remained high for a good long while (centuries? millennia?). Eventually, breeding with humans (for both Garou and Kin), not living up to your ancestors deeds, and/or switches tribes will all take it's toll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always though this as a chicken and egg dilema. Is the tribe that makes the totem or vice versa, in their story they said that in ancient times they took the best kin from the other tribes so the origin of purebreed wasnt that much of an issue for them. <br /> <br /> My advice is be consistent. Either the tribe makes the spirit, meaning the tribes view change and the spirit follow or the spirit has a set of values that might deffer from the tribe.<br /> <br /> For example. Maybe all falcon spirits are snotty eugenics fanatics and always have being or they are the ideal of the tribe and had come to tolerate the worse aspect of the silver fangs.<br /> <br /> We had a similar plot in a game, our dm say the SFs not only didnt accept him on the tribe but tried of kill him as to no devalue their purebreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}